<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">reduction-base</ansi> (cooking recipe)

A culinary reduction, cooked down slow over low heat until it turns
bitter, dark, and perfectly clarified, every impurity risen and skimmed
away twice over. It is not meant to be eaten on its own -- only to sit
at the bottom of something stronger, giving an unmaking draught its bite
and its clean, cold finish. Cooks who make it work with the windows
open.

